Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Error Payload",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 409
        },
        "message": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "details": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "resume_details": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "prefix_hash": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 64
                },
                "resume_token": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "resume_offset": {
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "resume_timestamp": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "date-time"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed using the Cyclic Redundancy Check (CRC) algorithm. The exact algorithm used is not specified in the context provided. However, it is recommended to use a recommended version of the CRC algorithm, such as the CRC-32 algorithm.
